<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <fullName>Total_Variance_Pct__c</fullName>
    <description>The dollar change against the prior bill expressed as a percentage of that prior bill. Pairs with the absolute figure so that a small bill doubling and a large bill moving a few percent can be told apart during the monthly review.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Percentage change against last month total charges. Blank on a first bill, and blank where last month total was zero, because a percentage change from zero has no meaning.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Total Variance Percent</label>
    <formula><![CDATA[IF( OR( ISBLANK(Prior_Utility_Bill__c), Prior_Utility_Bill__r.Total_Charges_Amount__c = 0 ), null, ( Total_Charges_Amount__c - Prior_Utility_Bill__r.Total_Charges_Amount__c ) / Prior_Utility_Bill__r.Total_Charges_Amount__c )]]></formula>
    <formulaTreatBlanksAs>BlankAsZero</formulaTreatBlanksAs>
    <precision>18</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>2</scale>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Percent</type>
    <!--
      🔴 CORRECTED 2026-08-22 — the previous version of this comment was empirically WRONG and
      caused a live 100x overstatement bug. A Percent FORMULA field IS already scaled by the
      platform for display, exactly like a Percent input field; it does not need a trailing * 100.
      Measured against usman-dpeg with real data (then rolled back): CURRENT=172.50, PRIOR=100.00
      gave Total_Variance_Amount__c=72.50 (correct) but Total_Variance_Pct__c=7250.00 (should be
      72.50) while the formula still had "* 100" appended. Removing "* 100" is the fix, confirmed
      by re-running the same scenario after deploy: Total_Variance_Pct__c=72.50.
      _Pct__c is the ARCHITECTURE section 1 suffix for a number that would otherwise read
      as categorical.
    -->
</CustomField>
